<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>1</b></sup> Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>2</b></sup> For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>3</b></sup> They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>4</b></sup> They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from <i>being</i> a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>5</b></sup> For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>6</b></sup> The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>7</b></sup> Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>8</b></sup> Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>9</b></sup> Do unto them as <i>unto</i> the Midianites; as <i>to</i> Sisera, as <i>to</i> Jabin, at the brook of Kison:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>10</b></sup> <i>Which</i> perished at Endor: they became <i>as</i> dung for the earth.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>11</b></sup> Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>12</b></sup> Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>13</b></sup> O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>14</b></sup> As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>15</b></sup> So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>16</b></sup> Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>17</b></sup> Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:<br />
<title canonical="true" type="psalm">A Song <i>or</i> Psalm of Asaph.</title><sup><b>18</b></sup> That <i>men</i> may know that thou, whose name alone <i>is</i> JEHOVAH, <i>art</i> the most high over all the earth. <br />
